100: The `styleSheet` attribute must return the associated cite217†CSS style sheet , if any, or null otherwise.\nL1101: The `layerName` attribute must return the cite614†layer name declared in the at-rule itself, or an empty string if the layer is anonymous, or null if the at-rule does not declare a layer.\nL1102: \nL1103: The `supportsText` attribute must return the cite615†<supports-condition> declared in the at-rule itself, or null if the at-rule does not declare a supports condition.\nL1104: \nL1105: Note: An `@import` at-rule might not have an associated cite217†CSS style sheet (e.g., if it has a non-matching `supports()` condition).\nL1106: \nL1107: Tests\nL1108:   * cite616†cssimportrule.html†wpt.fyi cite617†(live test)†wpt.live cite618†(source)†github.com L1109:   * cite619†cssimportrule-parent.html†wpt.fyi cite620†(live test)†wpt.live cite621†(source)†github.com L1110:   * cite622†cssimportrule-sheet-identity.html†wpt.fyi cite623†(live test)†wpt.live cite624†(source)†github.com L1111: #### 6.4.5. The `cite385†CSSGroupingRule ` Interface\nL1112: The `CSSGroupingRule` interface represents an at-rule that contains other rules nested inside itself.\nL1113: \nL1114:     [cite167†Exposed†webidl.spec.whatwg.org =Window]\nL1115:     interface `CSSGroupingRule` : cite323†CSSRule {\nL1116:       [cite306†SameObject†webidl.spec.whatwg.org ] readonly attribute cite325†CSSRuleList cite519†cssRules ;\nL1117:       cite171†unsigned long†webidl.spec.whatwg.org cite625†insertRule (cite169†CSSOMString `rule`, optional cite171†unsigned long†webidl.spec.whatwg.org `index` = 0);\nL1118:       cite174†undefined†webidl.spec.whatwg.org cite626†deleteRule (cite171†unsigned long†webidl.spec.whatwg.org `index`);\nL1119:     };\nL1120: The `cssRules` attribute must return a `CSSRuleList` object for the cite627†child CSS rules .\nL1121: \nL1122: The `insertRule(`rule`, `index`)` method must return the result of invoking cite339†insert a CSS rule `rule` into the cite627†child CSS rules at `index`, with the `nested` flag set.\nL1123: \nL1124: The `deleteRule(`index`)` method must cite376†remove a CSS rule from the cite627†child CSS rules at `index`.\nL1125: \nL1126: Tests\nL1127:   * cite628†CSSGroupingRule-cssRules.html†wpt.fyi cite629†(live test)†wpt.live cite630†(source)†github.com L1128:   * cite631†CSSGroupingRule-insertRule.html†wpt.fyi cite632†(live test)†wpt.live cite633†(source)†github.com L1165: The `style` attribute must return a `CSSPageDescriptors` object for the `@page` at-rule, with the following properties:\nL1166: \nL1167: cite600†computed flag L1168:     Unset.\nL1169: cite601†readonly flag L1170:     Unset.\nL1171: cite602†declarations L1172:     The declared descriptors in the rule, in cite603†specified order .\nL1173: cite604†parent CSS rule L1174:     cite605†this†webidl.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1175: cite606†owner node L1176:     Null.\nL1177: Tests\nL1178: \nL1179:   * cite641†cssom-pagerule.html†wpt.fyi cite642†(live test)†wpt.live cite643†(source)†github.com L1180: #### 6.4.8. The `cite573†CSSMarginRule ` Interface\nL1181: \nL1182: The `CSSMarginRule` interface represents a margin at-rule (e.g. `@top-left`) in an `@page` at-rule. cite644†[CSS3PAGE] L1183: \nL1184:     [cite167†Exposed†webidl.spec.whatwg.org =Window]\nL1185:     interface `CSSMarginRule` : cite323†CSSRule {\nL1186:       readonly attribute cite169†CSSOMString cite645†name ;\nL1187:       [cite306†SameObject†webidl.spec.whatwg.org , cite307†PutForwards†webidl.spec.whatwg.org =cssText] readonly attribute CSSMarginDescriptors cite646†style ;\nL1188:     };\nL1189: The `name` attribute must return the name of the margin at-rule. The `@` character is not included in the name. cite118†[CSS3SYN] L1190: \nL1191: The `style` attribute must return a `CSSMarginDescriptors` object for the margin at-rule, with the following properties:\nL1192: \nL1193: cite600†computed flag L1194:     Unset.\nL1195: cite601†readonly flag L1196:     Unset.\nL1197: cite602†declarations L1198:     The declared declarations in the rule, in cite603†specified order .\nL1199: cite604†parent CSS rule L1200:     cite605†this†webidl.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1201: cite606†owner node L1202:     Null.\nL1203: #### 6.4.9. The `cite530†CSSNamespaceRule ` Interface\nL1204: \nL1205: The `CSSNamespaceRule` interface represents an `@namespace` at-rule.\nL1206: \nL1207:     [cite167†Exposed†webidl.spec.whatwg.org =Window]\nL1208:     interface `CSSNamespaceRule` : cite323†CSSRule {\nL1209:       readonly attribute cite169†CSSOMString cite532†namespaceURI ;\nL1210:       readonly attribute cite169†CSSOMString cite531†prefix ;\nL1211:     };\nL1212: \nL1213: \nL1214: The `namespaceURI` attribute must return the namespace of the `@namespace` at-rule.\nL1215: The `prefix` attribute must return the prefix of the `@namespace` at-rule or the empty string if there is no prefix.\nL1216: \nL1217: Tests\nL1218: \nL1219:   * cite647†at-namespace.html†wpt.fyi cite648†(live test)†wpt.live cite649†(source)†github.com L1220:   * cite650†CSSNamespaceRule.html†wpt.fyi cite651†(live test)†wpt.live cite652†(source)†github.com L1221: ### 6.5. CSS Declarations\nL1222: \nL1223: A CSS declaration is an abstract concept that is not exposed as an object in the DOM. A cite653†CSS declaration has the following associated properties:\nL1224: \nL1225: property name\nL1226:     The property name of the declaration.\nL1227: value\nL1228:     The value of the declaration represented as a list of component values.\nL1229: important flag\nL1230:     Either set or unset. Can be changed.\nL1231: case-sensitive flag\nL1232:     Set if the cite654†property name is defined to be case-sensitive according to its specification, otherwise unset.\nL1233: ### 6.6. CSS Declaration Blocks\nL1234: \nL1235: A CSS declaration block is an ordered collection of CSS properties with their associated values, also named cite653†CSS declarations . In the DOM a cite655†CSS declaration block is a `CSSStyleDeclaration` object. A CSS declaration block has the following associated properties:\nL1394:   * cite769†cssstyledeclaration-setter-form-controls.html†wpt.fyi cite770†(live test)†wpt.live cite771†(source)†github.com L1395:   * cite772†cssstyledeclaration-setter-logical.html†wpt.fyi cite773†(live test)†wpt.live cite774†(source)†github.com L1396:   * cite775†page-descriptors.html†wpt.fyi cite776†(live test)†wpt.live cite777†(source)†github.com L1397:   * cite778†property-accessors.html†wpt.fyi cite779†(live test)†wpt.live cite780†(source)†github.com L1398: The object’s cite177†supported property indices†heycam.github.io are the numbers in the range zero to one less than the number of cite653†CSS declarations in the cite602†declarations . If there are no such CSS declarations, then there are no supported property indices.\nL1399: \nL1400: Getting the `cssText` attribute must run these steps:\nL1401: \nL1402:   1. If the cite600†computed flag is set, then return the empty string.\nL1403: \nL1404:   2. Return the result of cite514†serializing the cite602†declarations .\nL1405: Setting the `cite700†cssText ` attribute must run these steps:\nL1406: \nL1407:   1. If the cite601†readonly flag is set, then cite200†throw†heycam.github.io a `cite781†NoModificationAllowedError†webidl.spec.whatwg.org ` exception.\nL1408:   2. Empty the cite602†declarations .\nL1409:   3. cite541†Parse the given value and, if the return value is not the empty list, insert the items in the list into the cite602†declarations , in cite603†specified order .\nL1410:   4. cite782†Update style attribute for the cite655†CSS declaration block .\nL1411: The `length` attribute must return the number of cite653†CSS declarations in the cite602†declarations .\nL1412: \nL1413: The `item(`index`)` method must return the cite654†property name of the cite653†CSS declaration at position `index`. If there is no `index`th object in the collection, then the method must return the empty string.\nL1414: \nL1415: The `getPropertyValue(`property`)` method must run these steps:\nL1416:   1. If `property` is not a cite124†custom property , follow these substeps:\nL1417:     1. Let `property` be `property` cite147†converted to ASCII lowercase†infra.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1418:     2. If `property` is a shorthand property, then follow these substeps:\nL1419:       1. Let `list` be a new empty array.\nL1420:       2. For each longhand property `longhand` that `property` maps to, in canonical order, follow these substeps:\nL1421:         1. If `longhand` is a cite128†case-sensitive†w3c.github.io match for a cite654†property name of a cite653†CSS declaration in the cite602†declarations , let `declaration` be that CSS declaration, or null otherwise.\nL1422:         2. If `declaration` is null, then return the empty string.\nL1423:         3. Append the `declaration` to `list`.\nL1424:       3. If cite665†important flags of all declarations in `list` are same, then return the cite134†serialization of `list`.\nL1425:       4. Return the empty string.\nL1426:   2. If `property` is a cite128†case-sensitive†w3c.github.io match for a cite654†property name of a cite653†CSS declaration in the cite602†declarations , then return the result of invoking cite134†serialize a CSS value of that declaration.\nL1427:   3. Return the empty string.\nL1428: Tests\nL1506: The `parentRule` attribute must return the cite604†parent CSS rule .\nL1507: \nL1508: The `cssFloat` attribute, on getting, must return the result of invoking `cite703†getPropertyValue() ` with `float` as argument. On setting, the attribute must invoke `cite705†setProperty() ` with `float` as first argument, as second argument the given value, and no third argument. Any exceptions thrown must be re-thrown.\nL1519: Setting the cite814†`camel-cased attribute` attribute must invoke `cite705†setProperty() ` with the first argument being the result of running the cite815†IDL attribute to CSS property algorithm for `camel-cased attribute`, as second argument the given value, and no third argument. Any exceptions thrown must be re-thrown.\nL1520: \nL1521: For example, for the cite816†font-size property there would be a `fontSize` IDL attribute.\nL1522: For each CSS property `property` that is a cite125†supported CSS property and that begins with the string `-webkit-`, the following partial interface applies where `webkit-cased attribute` is obtained by running the cite807†CSS property to IDL attribute algorithm for `property`, with the lowercase first flag set.\nL1523: \nL1524:     partial interface cite578†CSSStyleProperties {\nL1527: The ``webkit-cased attribute`` attribute, on getting, must return the result of invoking `cite703†getPropertyValue() ` with the argument being the result of running the cite815†IDL attribute to CSS property algorithm for `webkit-cased attribute`, with the dash prefix flag set.\nL1528: Setting the cite817†`webkit-cased attribute`†www.w3.org attribute must invoke `cite705†setProperty() ` with the first argument being the result of running the cite815†IDL attribute to CSS property algorithm for `webkit-cased attribute`, with the dash prefix flag set, as second argument the given value, and no third argument. Any exceptions thrown must be re-thrown.\nL1529: For example, if the user agent supports the cite818†-webkit-transform†compat.spec.whatwg.org property, there would be a `webkitTransform` IDL attribute. There would also be a `WebkitTransform` IDL attribute because of the rules for camel-cased attributes.\nL1530: For each CSS property `property` that is a cite125†supported CSS property , except for properties that have no \"`-`\" (U+002D) in the property name, the following partial interface applies where `dashed attribute` is `property`.\nL1531: \nL1532:     partial interface cite578†CSSStyleProperties {\nL1533:       [cite699†CEReactions†html.spec.whatwg.org ] attribute [cite168†LegacyNullToEmptyString†webidl.spec.whatwg.org ] cite169†CSSOMString `_dashed_attribute`;\nL1534:     };\nL1535: The ``dashed attribute`` attribute, on getting, must return the result of invoking `cite703†getPropertyValue() ` with the argument being `dashed attribute`.\nL1536: \nL1537: Setting the cite819†`dashed attribute` attribute must invoke `cite705†setProperty() ` with the first argument being `dashed attribute`, as second argument the given value, and no third argument. Any exceptions thrown must be re-thrown.\nL1694: The `style` attribute must return a `cite578†CSSStyleProperties ` object whose cite601†readonly flag is unset, whose cite604†parent CSS rule is null, and whose cite606†owner node is cite605†this†webidl.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1695: \nL1696: If the user agent supports HTML, the following IDL applies: cite117†[HTML] L1697: \n"
